Specifically, the following pieces were lifted from omiGlass/firmware/ and
then rewritten for the ESP-IDF v5.2 toolchain (the upstream was Arduino / PlatformIO):

    - PDM microphone capture pattern (src/mic.cpp)
        -> ported to components/honest_mic/mic.c using the new
           driver/i2s_pdm.h API.

    - Opus encoder ring-buffer pattern (src/opus_encoder.cpp)
        -> scaffolded in components/honest_mic/opus_stub.c.
           Real Opus encoding is gated behind CONFIG_HONEST_PUCK_USE_OPUS
           and currently emits raw 16-bit PCM frames so the project builds
           without pulling a non-MIT/Apache dependency.

    - BLE GATT layout and UUIDs (src/app.cpp, src/config.h)
        -> ported to components/honest_ble/ble_audio.c using NimBLE.
           The 128-bit service UUID 19B10000-E8F2-537E-4F6C-D104768A1214 and
           the AUDIO_DATA / AUDIO_CODEC characteristics are preserved byte-
           for-byte so existing Omi-compatible clients (including the
           daemon Android app) pair with no protocol changes.

    - Audio packet framing (2 bytes index + 1 byte sub-index + payload)
        -> preserved in components/honest_ble/ble_audio.c.

What is ORIGINAL to Honest Puck (not from omi):

    - components/honest_ui/ (button debouncing + WS2812 privacy LED driver)
    - components/honest_mic/honest_gate.c (Si2301BDS PMOS load-switch interlock)
    - All pin mappings in main/honest_puck_pins.h
    - Project build system (CMakeLists.txt, sdkconfig.defaults)

